            "privateNotes": "",
            "publicNotes": "<p>Whether in pursuit of escaped prisoners, runaway debtors, or prodigal heirs, bounty hunters ruthlessly chase their prey for as long as the money's good. While many targets are wanted \"dead or alive,\" or plain and simply \"dead,\" the hunter below specializes in bringing targets back alive using their magbolas and shock weapons.</p><h2>Mercenaries</h2><p>So long as the almighty credit can buy power, safety, and comfort, it can also be used to buy violence from the desperate, irrational, and unsentimental. Absalom Station is home to countless mercenary companies and freelance soldiers-for-hire, all eagerly offering their services to the highest bidder.</p>\n<p>Some mercs have a moral code or sense of honor that limits what contracts they accept, and Absalom law strictly limits what jobs a paramilitary company can hand out to its members. Of course, this doesn't stop a festering underbelly of wetwork and worse from blooming in the darker reaches of the station, if one knows where to look.</p>\n<p>Mercenaries aren't always operatives or soldiers. Sometimes they're cunning spellcasters, powerful solarians, or treacherous envoys. Bounty hunters are one of the most common class of merc hanging around the station. The bounty hunter below is an example of an elite foe tracking down dangerous outlaws, but the statistics for gangsters can stand in for lower-level mercenaries.</p>",
            "publication": {
                "license": "ORC",
                "remaster": true,
                "title": "Starfinder Absalom Station"
            }
        },
